meta {
  name: Refresh Token
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/auth/refresh
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "refresh_token": "{{refresh_token}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200 && res.body && res.body.data) {
    bru.setEnvVar("access_token", res.body.data.access_token);
    bru.setEnvVar("refresh_token", res.body.data.refresh_token);
  }
}

docs {
  # POST /auth/refresh
  
  Rotate the access JWT using a valid refresh token. The previous refresh token is consumed and a new pair is issued.
  
  ## HTTP Method & Route
  - **Method:** `POST`
  - **Route:** `/wp-json/tutor/v1/auth/refresh`
  
  ## Authentication
  - **Type:** Public (refresh token in body)
  - **No API key or Bearer token required**
  
  ## Request Body
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
  | `refresh_token` | `string` | **Yes** | Refresh token from login (or prior refresh). |
  
  ## Responses
  
  ### 200 OK (Success)
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_auth_refresh",
    "message": "Token refreshed successfully.",
    "data": {
      "access_token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...",
      "expires_in": 86400,
      "refresh_token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...",
      "user_id": 1,
      "display_name": "Admin"
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ### 401 Unauthorized
  Invalid or expired refresh token.
  
  ### 403 Forbidden
  API key bound to the refresh session has been revoked.
}
